Z||000005||EdsB52||05-02-2001||08:16 PM||||That depends upon genetics. If your Fiero is a bastard with, let's say a jap car for a mother and a Pudstain (Mustang) deadbeat for a father, then your (hybrid) Fiero will grow with defiance and poor performance no matter how well you raise it. But if your Fiero is purebred with 88GT's for both parents then your child will probably raise itself and require very few parent/teacher conferences. Fortunately 4cyl's don't eat as much, so until it grows into a 6cyl, you probably won't have to invest as much.<p>[This message has been edited by EdsB52 (edited 05-02-2001).]||||reg||1
